{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '380,590p'\"","aggregated_output":"   380\t         :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n   381\t                        :closable)))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- install-more!\n   385\t  \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n   386\t   the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n   387\t   reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n   388\t   without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n   389\t   identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n   390\t   its own stream.\"\n   391\t  [link answer]\n   392\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)]\n   393\t    (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n   394\t           more (:dao.stream.remote/more answer)]\n   395\t      (when (and cur (seq more))\n   396\t        (let [[o & further] more]\n   397\t          (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]] o)\n   398\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- absorb!\n   402\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   403\t   id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n   404\t   reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n   405\t   reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n   406\t   descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n   407\t   emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n   408\t   filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n   409\t   id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n   410\t   reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n   411\t   stays outstanding -- and values that are not well-formed answers,\n   412\t   are dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   413\t  [link v]\n   414\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   415\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   416\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   417\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   418\t              req (:req entry)\n   419\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   420\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   421\t          (when (= (:dao.stream/identity v) (:identity @refl))\n   422\t            (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   423\t            (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   424\t            (cond\n   425\t              (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   426\t              (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   427\t                  (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   428\t                            (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   429\t                    (emit! link v)))\n   430\t\n   431\t              (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   432\t              ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   433\t              ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   434\t              (when (nil? e)\n   435\t                (learn! refl v)\n   436\t                (emit! link v))\n   437\t\n   438\t              (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   439\t              (emit! link v)\n   440\t\n   441\t              :else\n   442\t              (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   443\t                         [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   444\t                  (install-more! link v)))))))))\n   445\t\n   446\t\n   447\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   448\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   449\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   450\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   451\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   452\t  [link]\n   453\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   454\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   455\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   456\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   457\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   458\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   459\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   460\t\n   461\t\n   462\t(defn- retry-pending!\n   463\t  \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n   464\t   until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n   465\t   outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n   466\t  [link]\n   467\t  (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n   468\t    (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n   469\t\n   470\t\n   471\t(defn- drain!\n   472\t  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n   473\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n   474\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n   475\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n   476\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n   477\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n   478\t   one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n   479\t   is accepted.\"\n   480\t  [link]\n   481\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   482\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n   483\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n   484\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n   485\t    (retry-pending! link)\n   486\t    (loop []\n   487\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\n   488\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   489\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   490\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\n   491\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   492\t              (recur))\n   493\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   494\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n   495\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   496\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\n   497\t          nil)))))\n   498\t\n   499\t\n   500\t;; =============================================================================\n   501\t;; The reflection (2.4)\n   502\t;; =============================================================================\n   503\t\n   504\t(defn- result\n   505\t  [outcome]\n   506\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n   507\t\n   508\t\n   509\t(defn- refl-descriptor\n   510\t  \"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\n   511\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\n   512\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\n   513\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\n   514\t   channel loss.\"\n   515\t  [refl]\n   516\t  (drain! (:link @refl))\n   517\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   518\t   :dao.stream/descriptor (:descriptor @refl)\n   519\t   :dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)})\n   520\t\n   521\t\n   522\t(defn- surface-lacks?\n   523\t  \"True when the source's declared surface is learned and lacks the\n   524\t   surface `op` needs. Before the probe's answer the reflection\n   525\t   declares #{:reader :writer :closable}, so every operation is\n   526\t   attempted; an operation the source turns out to lack is answered as\n   527\t   the no-surface case.\"\n   528\t  [refl op]\n   529\t  (let [s (:surface @refl)]\n   530\t    (and (some? s) (not (contains? s (required-surface op))))))\n   531\t\n   532\t\n   533\t(defn- filed-answer-outcome\n   534\t  \"The outcome a filed answer yields: a protocol error translated per\n   535\t   the rules, otherwise the source's outcome map verbatim.\"\n   536\t  [ans]\n   537\t  (or (some-> (:dao.stream.remote/error ans) translated)\n   538\t      (bare-outcome ans)))\n   539\t\n   540\t\n   541\t(defn- filed-cursor\n   542\t  \"A filed answer for anchor `a` sent by `refl`, returned without\n   543\t   being forgotten: minting is idempotent, so the answer stays as true\n   544\t   as when it was minted.\"\n   545\t  [link refl a]\n   546\t  (when-some [[_ entry] (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)]\n   547\t    (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))\n   548\t\n   549\t\n   550\t(defn- filed-next!\n   551\t  \"A filed answer for cursor `c` sent by `refl`: the outcome an\n   552\t   installed more element put at `c` for the stream `refl` serves,\n   553\t   else the filed answer of a next request for `c`; returned and\n   554\t   forgotten.\"\n   555\t  [link refl c]\n   556\t  (let [k [(:identity @refl) c]]\n   557\t    (or (when-some [o (get (:filed-cursors @link) k)]\n   558\t          (swap! link update :filed-cursors dissoc k)\n   559\t          (filed-answer-outcome o))\n   560\t        (when-some [[id entry]\n   561\t                    (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/next c)]\n   562\t          (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\n   563\t          (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))))\n   564\t\n   565\t\n   566\t(defn- retry-read\n   567\t  \"The answer a just-sent cursor request gives: the source's map,\n   568\t   invalid-anchor included, arrives later as an answer.\"\n   569\t  []\n   570\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   571\t   :dao.stream/retry? true})\n   572\t\n   573\t\n   574\t(defn- send-or-count!\n   575\t  \"Send the request for `op` with `arg` when none of this reflection's\n   576\t   own is outstanding; otherwise count one further ask of the\n   577\t   outstanding request, which re-sends it at the link's resend-after\n   578\t   k.\"\n   579\t  [link refl op arg]\n   580\t  (if-some [id (outstanding-for link refl op arg)]\n   581\t    (count-ask! link id)\n   582\t    (send-request! link refl (wire-request link refl op [arg]))))\n   583\t\n   584\t\n   585\t(defn- refl-cursor\n   586\t  \"The cursor operation: a filed answer for the anchor is returned,\n   587\t   and a filed protocol error translated; otherwise a cursor request\n   588\t   is sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error\n   589\t   with :dao.stream/retry? true. Once closed, cursor answers closed;\n   590\t   once gone, transport-error naming not-found.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
