{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '60,310p'\"","aggregated_output":"    60\t(defn- well-formed-answer?\n    61\t  \"True when `v` is a well-formed answer: a map carrying the id and\n    62\t   the identity and either a protocol error or an outcome map.\"\n    63\t  [v]\n    64\t  (and (map? v)\n    65\t       (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)\n    66\t       (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n    67\t       (or (contains? protocol-errors (:dao.stream.remote/error v))\n    68\t           (stream/outcome-map? v))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- required-surface\n    72\t  \"The declared surface `op` needs, under the fixed mapping: cursor\n    73\t   and next need :reader, append! needs :writer, descriptor needs no\n    74\t   surface and is always answerable.\"\n    75\t  [op]\n    76\t  (case op\n    77\t    (:dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next) :reader\n    78\t    :dao.stream/append! :writer\n    79\t    nil))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- error-answer\n    83\t  \"The protocol-error answer shape, with the id and identity the\n    84\t   request carried.\"\n    85\t  [identity id e]\n    86\t  {:dao.stream/identity identity\n    87\t   :dao.stream.remote/id id\n    88\t   :dao.stream.remote/error e})\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t;; =============================================================================\n    92\t;; The mirror step (2.3)\n    93\t;; =============================================================================\n    94\t\n    95\t(defn- valid-budget?\n    96\t  \"True when the request carries the optional next-only budget as a\n    97\t   positive integer. Anything else ignores the budget, which is always\n    98\t   correct for a mirror.\"\n    99\t  [req]\n   100\t  (let [k (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)]\n   101\t    (and (integer? k) (pos? k))))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- chase\n   105\t  \"The budget chase: `outcome` is an ok from next; follow the successor\n   106\t   cursor through the same apply-request path at most k - 1 further\n   107\t   times, collecting the further outcome maps in order. The vector ends\n   108\t   at and includes the first non-ok outcome, so blocked, end and gap\n   109\t   reach the reader with the source's own recovery cursor.\"\n   110\t  [h ctx k outcome]\n   111\t  (loop [more [] cur (:dao.stream/cursor outcome) n 1]\n   112\t    (if (or (>= n k) (nil? cur))\n   113\t      more\n   114\t      (let [r (middleware/apply-request h ctx\n   115\t                                        {:dao.stream.remote/op\n   116\t                                         :dao.stream/next\n   117\t                                         :dao.stream.remote/args [cur]})]\n   118\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   119\t          (recur (conj more r) (:dao.stream/cursor r) (inc n))\n   120\t          (conj more r))))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- write-answer!\n   124\t  \"Append one answer value toward the asker. A value the channel cannot\n   125\t   carry (invalid-value) is answered with the oversize protocol error\n   126\t   in place of that element, the read not skipped and no cursor\n   127\t   advanced past it; any other refused write leaves the request\n   128\t   unanswered.\"\n   129\t  [chan-writer answer]\n   130\t  (let [r (stream/append! chan-writer answer)]\n   131\t    (when (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   132\t      (stream/append! chan-writer\n   133\t                      (error-answer (:dao.stream/identity answer)\n   134\t                                    (:dao.stream.remote/id answer)\n   135\t                                    :dao.stream.remote/oversize)))))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- answer!\n   139\t  \"The mirror's steps 1 to 4 for one well-formed request: look the\n   140\t   identity up in the table (not-found); check the op against the\n   141\t   entry's declared surface under the fixed mapping (no-surface);\n   142\t   answer descriptor from the entry's handle directly, adding the\n   143\t   declared surface, and apply cursor, next and append! through\n   144\t   apply-request with the channel context; append the answer with the\n   145\t   id and identity. For next with a budget k, and an ok first outcome,\n   146\t   the chase places the further outcomes under more.\"\n   147\t  [table chan-writer channel req]\n   148\t  (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity req)\n   149\t        id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)\n   150\t        op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   151\t        entry (get table identity)]\n   152\t    (if-not entry\n   153\t      (write-answer! chan-writer\n   154\t                     (error-answer identity id\n   155\t                                   :dao.stream.remote/not-found))\n   156\t      (let [h (:handle entry)]\n   157\t        (if (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   158\t          (write-answer!\n   159\t            chan-writer\n   160\t            (-> (stream/descriptor h)\n   161\t                (assoc :dao.stream.remote/id id\n   162\t                       :dao.stream/identity identity\n   163\t                       :dao.stream.remote/surface (:surface entry))))\n   164\t          (if-not (contains? (into #{} (:surface entry))\n   165\t                             (required-surface op))\n   166\t            (write-answer! chan-writer\n   167\t                           (error-answer identity id\n   168\t                                         :dao.stream.remote/no-surface))\n   169\t            (let [ctx {:dao.stream.remote/channel channel}\n   170\t                  outcome (middleware/apply-request h ctx req)\n   171\t                  more (when (and (= :dao.stream/next op)\n   172\t                                  (valid-budget? req)\n   173\t                                  (= :dao.stream/ok\n   174\t                                     (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   175\t                         (chase h ctx (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)\n   176\t                                outcome))\n   177\t                  answer (cond-> (assoc outcome\n   178\t                                        :dao.stream.remote/id id\n   179\t                                        :dao.stream/identity identity)\n   180\t                           (seq more) (assoc :dao.stream.remote/more\n   181\t                                             more))]\n   182\t              (write-answer! chan-writer answer))))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn mirror-step\n   186\t  \"The pure step a peer runs over a channel to answer requests against\n   187\t   its table: `(mirror-step table chan-reader cursor chan-writer) ->\n   188\t   cursor'`. For each request read from chan-reader at `cursor`, in\n   189\t   order, the four steps of 2.3 run; the mirror holds no state between\n   190\t   calls beyond the returned cursor. A value that is neither a\n   191\t   well-formed request nor a well-formed answer is dropped as malformed\n   192\t   wire input. The step stops when the channel reader answers blocked\n   193\t   or end; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the lost wire\n   194\t   values being lost. The mirror never constructs, parses or rewrites\n   195\t   a cursor, an anchor or an outcome: the served stream is the\n   196\t   original, its cursors, its positions, its gap, its end.\"\n   197\t  [table chan-reader cursor chan-writer]\n   198\t  (let [channel (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor chan-reader))]\n   199\t    (loop [cursor cursor]\n   200\t      (let [r (stream/next chan-reader cursor)]\n   201\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   202\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   203\t          (do (when (well-formed-request? (:dao.stream/value r))\n   204\t                (answer! table chan-writer channel\n   205\t                         (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   206\t              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n   207\t          :dao.stream/blocked cursor\n   208\t          :dao.stream/end cursor\n   209\t          :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   210\t          cursor)))))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t;; =============================================================================\n   214\t;; The link (2.4, 2.5)\n   215\t;; =============================================================================\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- new-link\n   218\t  \"One link per channel descriptor, shared by every reflection through\n   219\t   that channel. A link holds the channel writer; the channel reader\n   220\t   and the link's own cursor on it; the outstanding request ids with\n   221\t   the request each was sent for; the attach descriptor probes the\n   222\t   writer has refused, kept unsent with the reflection each was sent\n   223\t   for; filed answers keyed by id; the more outcomes installed at\n   224\t   their served identity and the cursor that precedes each; an\n   225\t   optional event writer; and the policy data -- the resend-after k\n   226\t   and the budget k stamped on next requests, both composition data.\"\n   227\t  [chan policy]\n   228\t  (atom {:reader (:reader chan)\n   229\t         :writer (:writer chan)\n   230\t         :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   231\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader chan) :dao.stream/oldest))\n   232\t         :outstanding {}\n   233\t         :pending {}\n   234\t         :filed {}\n   235\t         :filed-cursors {}\n   236\t         :events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)\n   237\t         :resend-after (:dao.stream.remote/resend-after policy)\n   238\t         :budget (:dao.stream.remote/budget policy)\n   239\t         :next-id 0\n   240\t         :channel-gone? false}))\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\t(defn- mint-id!\n   244\t  \"The next asker-minted id, unique per channel.\"\n   245\t  [link]\n   246\t  (let [n (:next-id @link)]\n   247\t    (swap! link assoc :next-id (inc n))\n   248\t    n))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- emit!\n   252\t  \"Append one event to the link's event writer when one is composed;\n   253\t   without an event writer the event is dropped.\"\n   254\t  [link v]\n   255\t  (when-some [w (:events @link)]\n   256\t    (stream/append! w v)))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn- register!\n   260\t  \"Record `req` as outstanding under its id, with the request it was\n   261\t   sent for, its ask count, and the reflection that sent it.\"\n   262\t  [link refl req]\n   263\t  (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n   264\t    (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id]\n   265\t           {:req req :asks 0 :reflection refl})\n   266\t    (swap! refl update :ids conj id)))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn- wire-request\n   270\t  \"One request map for the channel, its id asker-minted; a next\n   271\t   request carries the link's budget when one is composed.\"\n   272\t  [link refl op args]\n   273\t  (cond-> {:dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)\n   274\t           :dao.stream.remote/op op\n   275\t           :dao.stream.remote/args args\n   276\t           :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n   277\t    (and (= :dao.stream/next op) (some? (:budget @link)))\n   278\t    (assoc :dao.stream.remote/budget (:budget @link))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn- send-request!\n   282\t  \"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\n   283\t   outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a send the\n   284\t   writer refuses with full leaves the request unsent and nothing\n   285\t   outstanding, so the operation answers as though unanswered and the\n   286\t   next ask sends again. An attach descriptor probe the writer\n   287\t   refuses with full is kept on the link instead, unsent, one retry\n   288\t   per drain until a send is accepted. Returns the writer's outcome.\"\n   289\t  [link refl req]\n   290\t  (let [r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)\n   291\t        id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n   292\t    (cond\n   293\t      (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   294\t      (do (register! link refl req)\n   295\t          (swap! link update :pending dissoc id))\n   296\t\n   297\t      (and (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   298\t           (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op req)))\n   299\t      (swap! link assoc-in [:pending id]\n   300\t             {:req req :reflection refl}))\n   301\t    r))\n   302\t\n   303\t\n   304\t(defn- count-ask!\n   305\t  \"Count one further ask of the outstanding request `id`; on reaching\n   306\t   the link's resend-after k, re-send it once -- the same id, a\n   307\t   duplicate of an idempotent operation, which recomputes the same or a\n   308\t   later, equally true answer -- and start counting afresh. append! is\n   309\t   never re-sent: it never stays outstanding beyond its send.\"\n   310\t  [link id]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
